
## no architecture step: gate 2 is the first stop and approves the brief
$ prompt-render.sh gate2 rp issue=new
Gate 2 · rp · spec-diff.md rev 1, plan.summary.md rev 1 · fast lane
Goal: Register 65535 reads correctly.
Scenarios: 1 — S1
Entries: 1 changed — R1
Plan: 1 code stages.
Issue: new — Read register 65535
Confirm: nothing flagged
Approving will:
- approve the brief
- file the issue
- create worktree .claude/worktrees/rp on branch feat/rp
- create 2 stage cards and spawn the implementer at s0 (commits and pushes on green, no per-stage stop)
- next stop: gate 4
Options:
1. switch to the full lane
Answer: approve [<n>[: <value>] …] · change <what> · stop
user: approve
$ prompt-render.sh approved rp
approved spec-rev=1
$ card-move.sh rp inprogress

## one code stage, committed on green
$ card-move.sh rp.s0 inprogress
$ card-log.sh rp.s0 green
$ card-move.sh rp.s0 inreview
impl: status=inreview stage=s0 delta=0
$ card-log.sh rp.s0 commit=1b8d0dd
